   186	## Known gaps / follow-ups
   187	
   188	- The `defaultdict` factory is a stored value, not a callable. Invoking a
   189	  Redblue function from a native builtin would need a callback path back into
   190	  the interpreter and the VM; that is a separate concern. `collections.put`
   191	  remains the explicit write, and `SPEC.md` states the value-factory rule.
   192	- `list.shift` is a constant-time read and does not remove the first item; the
   193	  quadratic spelling is `skip(xs, 1)`. The test pins the storage-sharing
   194	  relationship, not a wall-clock time.
   195	- A deque's `kind` marker makes an ordinary record fail the module's own shape
   196	  check, but a caller who writes the marker by hand can still construct the
   197	  record shape. Every operation validates every node of both ends recursively
   198	  before returning a deque, so a forged record with a malformed node anywhere is
   199	  refused by the first operation rather than trusted. That validation makes an
   200	  operation linear in the deque's size; the structural sharing still keeps a
   201	  pop from rebuilding the untouched side, which the resource tests pin.
